\f1\b0  A metal roofing and gutter manufacturer known for the 
\f0\b LeafGuard one-piece gutter system
\f1\b0 . Englert has a facility in New Jersey and serves Eastern PA through dealers. They produce high-quality aluminum 
\f0\b gutter coil in numerous colors
\f1\b0  and have local contractors as authorized installers. Englert\'92s LeafGuard is sold directly to homeowners via franchises, but Englert also sells coil and standard gutter products to contractors. 
\f2\i Location:
\f1\i0  Perth Amboy, NJ (with sales reps covering PA).\
	\'95	
\f0\b Other Local Suppliers:
\f1\b0  Smaller outfits like 
\f0\b Wilhelm Spouting & Supply (Lebanon, PA)
\f1\b0  , 
\f0\b Alan Kunsman Roofing & Siding (Freemansburg, PA)
\f1\b0   (a regional supplier of roofing/gutter materials), and 
\f0\b RAF Gutter Supply (serving PA/MD/DC)
\f1\b0   offer additional channels. These players often carve out niches by focusing on specific locales or providing personalized service (e.g., RAF offers delivered gutter coil and parts in the Mid-Atlantic).\
	\'95	
\f0\b Regional Demand Trends:
\f1\b0  In Eastern PA and surrounding areas, 
\f0\b home improvement activity is a key driver
\f1\b0 . Many suburban homeowners are investing in exterior upgrades (new gutters, gutter guards, siding refresh) to improve curb appeal and reduce maintenance. The presence of many 
\f0\b historic homes
\f1\b0  (especially in cities like Philadelphia and older towns) creates demand for specialized gutter profiles like half-round and custom copper gutters in restoration projects. Additionally, the 
\f0\b rise of large franchise installers and marketing-driven gutter companies
\f1\b0  (e.g., LeafFilter, LeafGuard, etc.) in this region is raising homeowner awareness of gutter replacements and guards. These companies spend heavily on advertising in PA/NJ markets, indirectly boosting consumer interest and thereby demand that trickles down to local suppliers (even if the franchises source their own materials, they heighten the overall market activity).\
	\'95	
\f0\b Competition Intensity:
\f1\b0  The Eastern PA region is 
\f2\i highly competitive
\f1\i0  for gutter supply. Contractors have multiple options for sourcing materials (local wholesalers like Onsite or Central Aluminum, large distributors like ABC/Beacon, direct-from-manufacturer options via Spectra or Englert, and even big-box retailers for small jobs). Price competition is strong, and service (delivery speed, product availability) often differentiates suppliers. The market\'92s competitiveness benefits contractors (with generally lower prices and ready supply) but puts pressure on supplier margins.\
