\f1\b0  A prominent seamless gutter supplier with many branches (especially in the South and Midwest).\
	\'95	
\f0\b OmniMax International:
\f1\b0  Parent of brands like 
\f0\b Amerimax
\f1\b0  (which supplies gutters to Home Depot/retail and also OEMs). OmniMax is a big national player in aluminum gutters and accessories, though much of their product goes to retail DIY channels.\
	\'95	
\f0\b Englert Inc.:
\f1\b0  National presence in metal roofing and gutter systems (LeafGuard product has nationwide marketing).\
	\'95	
\f0\b Service Partners:
\f1\b0  Backed by top insulation manufacturer (TopBuild), with 75+ branches in the U.S. handling gutters and other products.\
\
These national players set the tone on pricing (due to their volume purchasing of aluminum and steel) and often introduce new products or programs that filter down to the regional level. For example, if raw material costs spike, manufacturers like Spectra or OmniMax will announce price increases that distributors then pass on. Conversely, if a national player introduces a new gutter guard technology or color trend, local suppliers often need to follow suit to meet customer expectations.\
